            <ArticleTitle>Tell Me About You: Experiences Teach a Nurse the Importance of Listeningg.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>13-14</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1188/17.CJON.13-14</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Unexpected cardiac issues at an early age inspired me to return to school to pursue a career in nursing. While in school, a close relationship with a family member facing a terminal cancer diagnosis gave me insight into the importance of listening as a tool for keeping patients safe and delivering the most appropriate care. These insights have shaped my career as I moved from student to RN to oncology nurse practitioner.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
